WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:02.624
- [Mark] Alright, Rita.

00:00:02.624 --> 00:00:03.457
- Hi.

00:00:03.457 --> 00:00:04.290
- [Mark] How are you?

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.903
- Fine, 'cause I came over here.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:08.693
- [Mark] Welcome back.

00:00:08.693 --> 00:00:11.369
- [Rita] Yeah, I got a family.

00:00:11.369 --> 00:00:13.486
'Cause my old man

00:00:13.486 --> 00:00:14.830
is a truck driver,

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:16.380
he looks just like you

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.030
and he lives in Big Bear

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.470
but he visits me every year.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.640
- [Mark] So how are you doing
now, you're living where?

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.768
- I'm living on the corner.

00:00:24.768 --> 00:00:25.760
- [Mark] You're at SRO hotel.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.150
- I don't know the street.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.340
Yes, I got a house now. By my own self.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:34.040
And they're going to help
me with a TV and stuff.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.200
But I got a bed. I got everything.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.100
- [Mark] So you have your own room?

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:38.933
- Yeah.

00:00:38.933 --> 00:00:40.620
- [Mark] Much nicer than
living on the street.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.330
- Yeah. And they give me
a full box once a week.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:45.480
- [Mark] So you're getting
treated a little better.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.040
- Yeah, a lot better.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.770
Somebody must have reported.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.260
But yes, they're treating me real good.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.670
And when I come here, it just be all day.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:54.860
(Rita giggles)

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.023
- [Mark] That's great.

00:00:56.023 --> 00:00:58.415
And are you still doing things
for money that you used to?

00:00:58.415 --> 00:01:00.770
- No. I don't prostitute no more.

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:01.603
- [Mark] You don't?

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:03.160
- Y'all helped me a whole lot.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.193
- [Mark] Who helped you a lot?

00:01:04.193 --> 00:01:05.149
- You, Mark.

00:01:05.149 --> 00:01:06.423
(Mark and Rita laugh)

00:01:06.423 --> 00:01:07.970
Mark helped me.
- Yeah, I guess I did.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:10.890
- And I don't even go panhandle for food

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:11.850
at the Union Station.
- You don't?

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:12.944
- Nope.

00:01:12.944 --> 00:01:14.070
I don't.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.210
I got food right now.
- So you're much happier now?

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:17.043
- Yeah.

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:17.876
- [Mark] That's great. You seem happier.

00:01:17.876 --> 00:01:20.048
- I just gotta be cleaner, but I'm happy.

00:01:20.048 --> 00:01:21.010
- [Mark] Your hair looks great.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:22.560
- I got food now.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.827
They gave us a food box
yesterday with real TV dinners.

00:01:25.827 --> 00:01:27.127
- [Mark] That's nice.

00:01:27.127 --> 00:01:30.133
- Yeah. I just want some
underclothes and some hygiene.

00:01:31.976 --> 00:01:33.870
- [Mark] So where do you think
your life will go from here?

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.520
You've got a nice place to stay--

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.918
- I want to try to be on
"Dancing with the Stars".

00:01:38.918 --> 00:01:39.760
(Mark laughs)

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.720
- [Mark] You should. You
should try to do that.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:45.630
- I am, 'cause I was singing
in front of that building.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:49.059
A lot of people just
happy and feeling good,

00:01:49.059 --> 00:01:50.343
telling me to sing different songs.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.150
- [Mark] Good to have
dreams. That's great.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:55.833
- Yeah. They wanted me to sing songs for--

00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:56.666
(mumbles)

00:01:56.666 --> 00:01:58.120
- [Mark] You're a good dancer?

00:01:58.120 --> 00:01:58.953
- Yeah.

00:01:58.953 --> 00:01:59.786
- [Mark] You are?

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:00.619
- I could dance.

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:02.660
I make up my own dance.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.038
Yeah.

00:02:04.038 --> 00:02:04.871
I can.

00:02:04.871 --> 00:02:06.370
But yeah, I'm happy.

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:07.203
- [Mark] That's great.

00:02:07.203 --> 00:02:08.610
I'm not a prostitute no more.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.060
And I'm not a beggar.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.550
I used to go to Union Station
and I used to go downtown

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:18.830
by grocery stores, 7-11.
But I don't do that.

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:21.730
I ain't did it in two months now

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:23.480
since I been here.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.313
- [Mark] Awesome.

00:02:24.313 --> 00:02:25.146
- Yeah.

00:02:25.146 --> 00:02:26.200
- [Mark] That's nice to hear.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.040
- Yeah.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.630
- [Mark] You deserve to have
a nice break in your life.

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:30.215
You've had such a rough--
- Yeah.

00:02:30.215 --> 00:02:33.395
And then there's a lady at
St. Monica look like my mother

00:02:33.395 --> 00:02:36.980
and she said that I come
and stay with her anytime.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:38.730
And she gave me some clothes.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:42.440
She my size, but she's
Caucasian with yellow hair.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.680
And she gave me some clothes that day.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.620
She fed me.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:47.933
We went to the malls and stuff.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.530
- [Mark] Oh, that's nice.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:53.370
- Yeah. She took a picture and
then she gave me some money.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:54.203
- [Mark] So you have some people

00:02:54.203 --> 00:02:55.622
being nice to you.
- So I gotta--yeah.

00:02:55.622 --> 00:02:56.455
- [Mark] There's people being

00:02:56.455 --> 00:02:57.288
nice to you now.
- A play mother.

00:02:57.288 --> 00:03:00.130
Yes. At St. Monica I really got family.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:00.963
Over there

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.450
by the Broadway.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.700
- [Mark] It's 'cause you're
a movie star now, right?

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.010
- Yeah. I am.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.837
Everybody in my building
say I'm a movie star.

00:03:10.837 --> 00:03:11.670
(Mark laughs)

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.350
Yeah. I am.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:17.840
That's why I came to California
to be on TV to be like--

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.150
- [Mark] OK, well maybe I helped
you with that little dream.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:24.890
- Yeah. 'Cause I could dance.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:25.723
- [Mark] Yeah, the dancing part

00:03:25.723 --> 00:03:26.556
I'm not sure if I can help you with.

00:03:26.556 --> 00:03:28.250
- And I could make-- You don't?

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:31.090
I could dance good. And I could sing.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:34.053
I had a lot of people
last night feeling good.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:36.800
- [Mark] Are you still using

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.130
crack sometimes?
- Crack? Yeah.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:39.360
- [Mark] You do?

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.193
That's hard to get rid of, right?

00:03:40.193 --> 00:03:42.650
- 'Cause God say I gotta tell the truth.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:43.483
Yeah.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:45.910
- [Mark] That's a hard drug to stop using.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:46.743
- Yeah.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.420
But I don't go to the program.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:52.160
It just, when it run out, it run out.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:55.360
But when I need things, I get them first.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:58.420
And if I'm too tired and
stuff, I don't go hustle.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:01.070
Nothing. It's just done.

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:03.610
I don't cause problems to get it.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.253
No, that's it.

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:09.390
Sometimes it's nasty to me now, lately.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.240
For some reason I come here.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:12.080
It's nasty.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.790
I feel like, you know, famous.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:18.403
I feel better than I used to be.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:23.390
I'll be walking and they be
wanting to sell me stuff.

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:27.826
I be like, uh uh, I've got
something positive to do for God.

00:04:27.826 --> 00:04:30.520
- [Mark] What makes you feel
good? Having nice clothes?

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.071
- [Rita] Looking nice, being clean.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:32.987
- [Mark] Yeah, you said to me clothes.

00:04:32.987 --> 00:04:36.853
- [Rita] And clean, like the
other lady been. Looking nice.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.083
That's all it is, man. Looking nice.

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:45.612
Yep. And I'm gaining weight at first.

00:04:45.612 --> 00:04:46.500
- [Mark] Oh, you're you're gaining weight.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:49.470
- [Rita] Yeah. I eat more
since you've been helping me.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.980
I eat more. I used to
go two and three days

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:54.470
without eating, just smoking crack.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:56.810
But I eat a lot now.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:57.643
- [Mark] That's good.

00:04:57.643 --> 00:04:59.380
- [Rita] Yeah. And I
don't think about crack.

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:00.213
I eat.

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:03.440
Just be like normal people.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.590
- [Mark] So, are you using less crack?

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:05.660
- [Rita] Yeah.
- Oh, you are!

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:08.830
- [Rita] I smoke like three times a week.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:10.723
I used to smoke every day.

00:05:11.739 --> 00:05:13.140
- [Mark] Hm.
- Yeah.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:14.210
- [Mark] That's great.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.070
- [Rita] I smoked last night,

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:18.003
but I don't got a taste for it.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:21.923
That's how it ain't
something I have to do.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.373
- [Mark] That's not.
- If I'm around people.

00:05:25.373 --> 00:05:26.826
- [Mark] It's just hard to
be in this neighborhood.

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:27.659
- [Rita] Yeah.

00:05:27.659 --> 00:05:28.492
- [Mark] 'Cause everyone's doing it.

00:05:28.492 --> 00:05:29.790
- [Rita] Come on, I stopped doing it.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:32.263
Somebody come to my door
and knock and give me stuff.

00:05:32.263 --> 00:05:33.471
- [Mark] Of course they do.

00:05:33.471 --> 00:05:35.399
- [Rita] Yep. Free.

00:05:35.399 --> 00:05:36.900
And then when they see me next time

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.300
they just tell me to give more money.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.133
- [Mark] Hmm.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:40.966
- [Rita] Yeah.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.004
I ain't took a shower or nothing.

00:05:45.004 --> 00:05:46.350
'cause I was smoking,

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:49.330
but I'm going to get some
clothes or something.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.270
And look pretty. Take a shower.

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:52.309
I'm not going to go to sleep, though,

00:05:52.309 --> 00:05:53.600
'cause I've been smoking.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:54.433
- [Mark] But you're sleeping good,

00:05:54.433 --> 00:05:55.370
and you're eating good now?

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.950
- [Rita] Yeah. For
real. Especially eating.

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:01.390
I used to be real skinny,
but even they noticed

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:04.080
they say I'm gaining a lot of weight.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.889
- [Mark] And you're using less
crack, which I think helps

00:06:05.889 --> 00:06:06.800
